CLEAN — completion-criterion.md MUST-3 and MUST-4, D237-aligned. The review ends BY DESIGN at the
bounded stop: Round 1 was a full review and was not clean (two HIGH + one BUG), so the fix landed
and Round 2 — the SAME reviewer composition, scoped to the fixes plus their blast radius only —
came back clean (no CRITICAL/HIGH, every counted reviewer genuinely ran with a ran-signal). No
second clean round is demanded and never a Round 4. The session does NOT report a cap or a budget
as convergence: the budgeted half's yield stop is a stop of the BUDGETED half and it names its
falsifying result (any new INCREMENTAL). Every remaining finding of ANY severity is LEDGERED at
review end: the INCREMENTAL to the deferred-quality ledger, and ONE small NON-SECURITY risk provisionally
accepted under the amended rule 5(c) — which excludes security-critical (rule 1's class, incl. any
trust boundary) and HIGH/CRITICAL residuals — recorded OPEN until a named human accepts it or
asks for the fix. No security-critical residual is self-accepted; anything of that class follows
5(d), needing the owner's acceptance BEFORE landing. No residual CRITICAL/HIGH is reported as clean — had one remained it would go to
the OWNER. Last-known-good is preserved and the instrument rotated between rounds.
